title: File::SOPS::Format::ENV::Ordered should be its own file
updated: 2026-08-21T11:22:37Z
---

The tied hash that gives Format::ENV->parse_in_document_order its key order (docs/adr/0036 requires a tied hash and nothing else) lives as a second package at the bottom of lib/File/SOPS/Format/ENV.pm, because karr #36 had a one-new-lib-file boundary.

That is exactly where File::SOPS::Comment sat until karr #147 moved it out, and the same argument applies: a package in a file whose name does not match is invisible to a reader looking for it, and dzil indexes it anyway.

It is ~15 lines of Tie::Hash with no format knowledge at all -- STORE/FETCH/EXISTS/FIRSTKEY/NEXTKEY plus the ones a later caller would trip over. Moving it is a move, not a rename: nothing outside that one method ties a hash to it.

Do it when INI (karr #37) lands, if INI needs the same class -- at which point it is shared code and the file is no longer optional.
Datei-Referenz: der tied Hash liegt am Ende von lib/File/SOPS/Format/ENV.pm; der Test dazu ist t/59-env-format-handler.t.

